<title>ITALY: TIM net profit 930.2 bln lire in 1996.</title>
<headline>TIM net profit 930.2 bln lire in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     930.2 vs   (350.3)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     7,347.5 vs (2,800.5)</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	   3,231.8 vs (1,255.6)</p>
<p>    Ord div		  50 lire per share vs 10 lire</p>
<p>    Savings share div    51 lire per share vs 11 lire</p>
<p>Note - Telecom Italia Mobile is controlled by state telecom holding Stet. - The 1995 results are not comparable because they only start from July 14, the date when TIM was spun away from fixed line operator Telecom Italia.  </p>
<p>    Pretax profit			1,980.2 vs  (645.3)</p>
<p>    Net credit			     476.7 vs (-206.9)</p>
<p>    Operating result		   2,038.3 vs  (681.6)</p>
<p>    Invested capital		   1,480.4 vs 1,306.5</p>
<p>    Technical investments	    1,282   vs (n/g)</p>
<p>Note - TIM said it had over six million clients, with 1.9 million subscribers to its digital GSM service at end 1996. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
